## Campus Share SWOT Analysis

1. STRENGTHS

Unique Request + Giveaway model encourages active participation
Promotes peer-to-peer academic collaboration
Centralized, structured access to study resources
Directly addresses student challenges (resource gaps, disorganization)
Scalable across modules, faculties, and institutions

2. WEAKNESSES

Depends on consistent user engagement and contributions
Initial cold start problem (limited resources at launch)
Requires moderation to maintain content quality
Request tab may become cluttered without proper filtering
Slightly increased system complexity due to dual features

3. OPPORTUNITIES

Expansion into a full academic support ecosystem (forums, tutoring)
Potential partnerships with universities or student organizations
Integration of AI-based recommendations
Development of a mobile application
Use of platform data to identify high-demand modules/resources
Gamification (badges, contributions tracking) to boost engagement

4. THREATS

Competition from informal platforms (WhatsApp, Google Drive, Telegram)
Copyright and academic integrity concerns
Risk of low participation (users consume but don’t contribute)
Data privacy and security risks
Possible misuse (spam requests or irrelevant uploads

5. STRATEGIC INSIGHT

The Request + Giveaway system transforms the platform from a passive repository into a demand-driven academic network, increasing engagement and improving long-term sustainability.
